# Test-only dependencies. Edit this file, then regenerate the lock from the
# repository root:
#
#   uv pip compile --python-version 3.12 --generate-hashes --output-file requirements-dev.lock requirements-dev.in
#
# Install with hashes enforced, as the images do:
#
#   pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-dev.lock
#
# --python-version 3.12 is the minor version of the base image (the FROM line
# of both Dockerfiles). Patch updates need nothing here; a new minor means
# recompiling this lock and the two image locks.
#
# The image locks are constraints: any package shared with them (cryptography,
# cffi, pycparser, packaging) resolves to the exact version the images run, so
# the tests exercise the same AES-GCM implementation. Regenerate this lock
# whenever an image lock changes.

-c consumer/requirements.lock
-c producer/requirements.lock

# torch, transformers, huggingface_hub and kubernetes are absent on purpose:
# they are imported inside the functions that use them, and the unit tests
# stub those functions instead.

cryptography
pytest
pytest-cov
ruff==0.16.8
